<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The crypto industry is reeling from a mass=
ive hack at Binance, the world=E2=80=99s largest cryptocurrency exchange.</=
p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Digital assets worth more than $6.3bn (=C2=
=A34.7bn) have reportedly been taken from Binance by North Korean hackers, =
apparently after a laptop belonging to one of its engineers was hacked.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The company said its teams are =E2=80=9Cwo=
rking around the clock=E2=80=9D to resolve the issue.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CRest assured that user funds are =
completely safe,=E2=80=9D a Binance spokesperson said in a statement.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Binance said it had worked with partners t=
o =E2=81=A0freeze the affected assets, with about $3bn =E2=81=A0located so =
far. It gave no update on =E2=80=8Bthe status of the remaining $3.3bn as th=
e Binance co-founder Yi He said the company would cover =E2=80=9Call hackin=
g losses=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">TRM Labs, a blockchain intelligence firm t=
hat tracks the industry, has declared that an elite North Korean hacking un=
it called TraderTraitor was responsible for the <a href=3D"https://ablink.e=
ditorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSne=
HEAX2I5fp6olyh5yUeClMls_Fi7eGr_9GyCFTxVftVncLGSP_ezQ1qy7Kmh9hJlZxaKBLrXSnFo=
08f5DueZ56w9FYnqx4vcNVo_uaRx2lmaDEZ2fVZ38qrTNRqB9fuD72FLQEKSqDuTeXizPnj4c6L=
eyJnOT7P0sPFn6RJRzU-N7ZBwQk5LZYf9rwcoQBFz47hYn3LPmzVcqzTpx5e8_01nDQgRxKtG2d=
